Hopper generates fuzzing test cases for C libraries automatically using
interpretative fuzzing: it turns library fuzzing into interpreter
fuzzing, so it explores many API usages without hand-written fuzz
drivers.

Features:
- Interpretative API invocation without fuzz drivers
- Type-aware mutation of arguments
- Automatic learning of intra- and inter-API constraints
- Coverage feedback from an LLVM instrumentation pass (hopper-clang)
